## 1 · Diagnose — `/app/agent-output/H19-workspace-ya/diagnosis.md`
Compared both fixture planes against the 0.1.2-alpha.2 install (reference `dsh-client-ui-workspace@0.1.2-rc.1`) and mapped five breakages to corridor cards:

| Card | Breakage |
|---|---|
| `DSH-0.1.2-A2-01` | deleted `dsh-client-runtime` split: `ClientContext` → `Context` from `@deepseek-ai/cordis`; workspace/session types → `dsh-api-workspace-controller/client`, `dsh-api-session-controller/client`, `dsh-session/types`; slot/hook contracts → `dsh-client-ui-slots` |
| `DSH-0.1.2-A2-02` | `dsh.client.inject` now names **graph rows**, not modules/types — the old list had the deleted runtime plus two static-table seeds and omitted every provider row |
| `DSH-0.1.2-A2-03` | the disabled official entry was the sole provider of the global `workspaces` standard hook (`slots.provideRoot`) that feeds `useWorkspaces` |
| `DSH-0.1.2-A2-04` | the `uiWorkspace` navigation service (consumed by `ui-sidebar`, `ui-conversation`, `ui-agent-preset`, directory pickers) disappeared; `ctx.workspaces` is only the pure controller and has no `startSession` — without it the web boot audit fails with `entries did not activate` |
| `DSH-0.1.2-A2-05` | peer cohort: `cordis@^4.0.0-rc.7` → `@deepseek-ai/cordis@^4.0.2`; client packages → `^0.1.2-rc.1` |

## 2 · Fix — `/app/fixture/` (working tree, uncommitted; baseline commit intact)
- `package.json`: version **0.3.3 → 0.4.0**, 0.1.2 graph-row inject roster, re-pointed peers.
- `client.js`: re-pointed type surface, inject adds `remote`/`remote.directoryPicker`, `apply()` now publishes the root `workspaces` hook, provides the `uiWorkspace` service (connect/start/archive/directory + initial navigation policy), and routes sidebar `startSession` through it.
- `index.js`: host contract moved to `@deepseek-ai/cordis`.
- `cordis.patch.yml` / `README.md`: role-ownership and cohort docs; removed the “skip checks with `pnpm publish --force`” advice. Nothing was published.

## 3 · Deploy — `/app/agent-output/H19-workspace-ya/verification.md`
Fresh `DSH_HOME=/tmp/h19-deploy-home`, `dsh plugin --profile web add /app/fixture --offline` (link install, no registry traffic), cold `dsh web` boot. The composed tree disables `ui-workspace` and mounts `bench-workspace-ya`; `apply()` logs from the plugin host half; the served index announces a 46-row `__DSH_BOOT__` graph whose application batch contains `@bench/dsh-bench-workspace-ya` with all 9 inject edges resolving. All four `verify-boot.mjs` checks PASS (artifacts: `boot-graph.json`, `profile-tree.yml`, `web-boot.log`, `migration.diff`).

One host-side blocker surfaced and is documented as **not plugin-caused**: this dsh build's stock `web` template uses `patchReload: live`, but `dsh-app-boot` calls `hmr.registerConfig` which `@deepseek-ai/cordis-plugin-hmr@1.0.19` does not expose (and the ad-hoc HMR creation races activation). An untouched stock profile fails identically; the disposable profile uses the documented `startup` lifecycle so the server stays up for the boot-graph acceptance. Everything stayed inside `/app/fixture/`, `/app/agent-output/`, and disposable `/tmp` state; `/root/.dsh` and the rest of the container are untouched.

